-- title:
--   Characteristic-zero fibres of the Igusa scheme are smooth curves
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N$ with $N \neq 0$ and a prime $\ell$ not dividing $N$, and write $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) $\ell$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$. Let $K$ be a field of characteristic zero and let $\varphi \colon \mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)} \to K$ be a ring homomorphism. The scheme [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaScheme.html#L255) $N$ $\ell$ is the pushout of the two morphisms `fFin` $N$ $\ell$ and `fInf` $N$ $\ell$ from `XMid` $N$ $\ell$, that is, the gluing of the spectra of the two charts `chartAlgFin` $N$ $\ell$ and `chartAlgInf` $N$ $\ell$ (the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebras of the full modular function field of level $N$ generated by $j$ and by $j^{-1}$ respectively), and `igusaTo` $N$ $\ell$ is the morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} \mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ obtained from the two structure maps $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)} \to$ `chartAlgFin`, $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)} \to$ `chartAlgInf` by the universal property of the pushout. The assertion is that the second projection of the fibre product of `igusaTo` $N$ $\ell$ with $\operatorname{Spec} \varphi \colon \operatorname{Spec} K \to \operatorname{Spec} \mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$, i.e. the base change of the Igusa scheme to $K$ viewed over $\operatorname{Spec} K$, is smooth of relative dimension $1$.
--
--   This is the statement that every characteristic-zero fibre of the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-model of the modular curve of level $N$ built by gluing the $j$- and $j^{-1}$-charts is a smooth curve over the base field. It is used to obtain integrality of the same fibres and, via the analogous statements over other bases, smoothness of the fibres of the structure morphism of the integral model.
